   "source": [
    "# What is aliasing ?\n",
    "\n",
    "'''\n",
    "Aliasing in Python occurs when two or more variables refer to the same object in memory. This means that changing \n",
    "the object through one variable also affects the other variable because they both point to the same object.\n",
    "'''"
   ]
  }
